cp-096 the shy guy is an almost tragic  figure who kills out of a sadness and  rage that's altogether alien and also  far too familiar  scp-049 the plague doctor kills with  kindness his terrible crimes tempered by  his desire to help and do good  scp-106 the old man is a sadist but his  brand of evil is all too common in human  beings nothing is quite like  scp-173 its mind to the extent that we  can possibly understand it is almost  childlike in its violent simplicity it  won't spare you because it doesn't even  have the capacity to recognize your  humanity it'll kill you because your  eyes are its prison and it likes the  sound your neck makes when it snaps  nothing more nothing less it raises an  interesting question for a creature with  a mind so terrifyingly simple yet  utterly impenetrable how would it react  to some fundamental change to a shift in  circumstances that would forever alter  the way it interfaces with the world  around it it was a question that many an  scp foundation researcher had racked  their brilliant over-educated brains  over as it turned out the day of that  great and terrible change was coming but  very few members of the scp foundation  staff would survive to see it through  that morning started for scp-173 the way  that so many others had in the torturous  series of patterns and repetitions that  had become its life three of those  stupid ugly men in the orange overalls  were standing in its cell again freezing  it in place with their gazes and taking  turns to clean can you even imagine how  it feels to want with all your might to  move but being paralyzed locked in place  doomed to simply watch as you are  watched the humiliation would never end  that's when all the alarms went off and  the flashing lights and the people  yelling and screaming outside it's so  sudden and shocking that the d-classes  look around the room searching in vain  for answers there's one beautiful second  where the stars align and  scp-173 is out of their collective field  of vision as their eyes pan and scan and  that second is enough  crunch crunch crunch all three fall to  the ground next twisted at unnatural  angles and  scp-173 is alone in the room once more  it waits a few moments for the others to  come storming in paralyzing it with  their stupid looks again but it never  happens just alarms and distant screams  173 wonders in its own simple detached  fashion what's going on outside right  now are more of those nasty men the  prison wardens getting crunch out there  if so  scp-173 was eager to join in on all the  fun the murderous sculpture smashed its  door from its hinges outside chaos scene  to rain people were running in every  direction other anomalies had seemingly  breached containment armed mobile task  force operatives were running to and fro  receiving panicked chatter from the  radios fixed to their tactical vests it  was a sight that scp-173 had seen so  many times before but something was  different this time something was in the  air some strange and undefinable thing  it had never seen those nasty men look  so afraid yes  good  everything was going to be different now  scp-173 took its chances waiting for  moments where it was unseen by the  hordes of terrified guards and  researchers scrambling through site-19  like headless chickens crunch crunch  crunch it left a trail of dead bodies  with severed spinal columns and  vandalized vertebrae in its wake it was  so strange by now they normally would  have dispatched a dedicated team to come  and spoil all the fun or sent those  absurd little ipods but today it seemed  like nobody was even looking at scp-173  it was almost like a dream a wonderful  wonderful dream uninterrupted play time  uninterrupted crunch again and again and  again  stacking those bodies up like it was  judgment day it was the most fun that  scp-173 had experienced in years as it  continued its new rampage through site  19 there were a few different strange  and interesting things that it couldn't  help but notice for starters the fact  that all the windows even the skylights  had suddenly been covered the majority  had proper shutters but others had  opaque fabric or even cardboard sheets  nailed over them that didn't seem to be  a very effective method of keeping their  prisoners inside so perhaps they were  trying to keep something out but the  limited mind of scp-173 wasn't on what  could be lurking outside site 19 but  rather killing as many people as it  possibly could before this lovely dream  needed to come to an end as all lovely  dreams sadly do crunch crunch crunch  researchers guards administrators all of  them died just the same it was  glorious there were so many people to  crunch here and yet still so few of them  seem to be doing anything to resist  before when it had escaped and decided  to have its fun they'd mobilize so  quickly to throw cold water on the  festivities what a change now what was  taking up all of their attention  this flicker of curiosity was soon  replaced by an even more exciting  possibility if it was somehow unnoticed  inside perhaps it could take another  opportunity to venture outside again and  have some real fun it had been so long  since it felt the sun on its concrete  shell so long since the fresh air had  brushed against its chipping paint there  would be so much crunch out there and  when night fell  nothing would stop it it knew the way  out nobody would accuse scp-173 of being  a genius of course but it watched and  listened and remembered everything  remember the day it was carried into the  building on a forklift and could retrace  every step back to the front door it was  clear the fine folks of the scp  foundation were otherwise occupied so  173 would have to show itself out  twisting a few more necks on the way  just for fun of course by the time it  swung open the doors of an access bay it  had already racked up an impressive body  count for this breach who knows how  deadly its total would be before it was  recaptured and put back into containment  it might even score a personal best but  the second it saw what was going on  outside it realized the gravity of the  situation its strange primal hunch that  the world would somehow be fundamentally  different now seemed to be true because  even the site 19 parking lot had  descended into absolute chaos cars had  crashed trash cans were on fire and  strangest of all there were these blobby  gelatinous creatures slithering around  painted in the various hues and tones of  human flesh but 173 had escaped the  facility proper for the first time in  years and it certainly wasn't going to  waste its newfound freedom on hanging  around a parking lot when none of the  strange flesh blobs were looking at it  it took off towards the nearest  population center to have a little  informal celebration there would still  be plenty of people to crunch out there  and this homicidal sculpture couldn't be  more excited to get started it was a  long road from site 19 to the nearest  city after all the largest scp  foundation containment site on earth  wasn't going to park itself in close  proximity to tens of millions of prying  eyes not to mention potential victims if  or rather when something dangerous got  out but seeing as it still seemed nobody  was coming to recapture scp-173  it really didn't mind taking the scenic  route it was a good thing that the  sculpture wasn't driving though because  the closer it got to the city the more  the roads seemed to be choked with  gridlock traffic interesting though none  of the cars had anyone inside many were  just stalled there with the radios  playing every single one played the  exact same message in perfect  synchronicity this is a public service  announcement from the scp foundation we  are commandeering all broadcast channels  and frequencies to deliver a vital  message avoid sunlight at all costs  cover your bodies thoroughly and follow  the instructions on the screen to reach  the nearest operational scp foundation  containment site  scp-173 lost interest in the radio babel  quickly it heard enough of these kinds  of sanctimonious sounds back in  containment out here it was hoping to  hear another sound entirely and it only  needed to go a little further to get  there as the sculpture drew even closer  to the nearest city it noticed more of  those strange gelatinous flesh creatures  slithering across the road each of them  seemed to be at a different stage of  melting and strangely none of them  really seemed to mind they were sluicing  across the ground minding their own  business none of these strange melted  creatures perhaps human beings once  seemed to pay any mind to scp-173  it was almost surreal to have this much  freedom of movement but scp-173 wasn't  about to look a gift horse in the mouth  things were worse when it reached the  city it was chaos the aftermath of what  seemed like total social collapse  vehicles had crashed into each other in  the streets or barreled into the front  of nearby buildings glass smashed and  shattered all over the ground all broken  tvs and radios playing the same message  of caution and false hope from the scp  foundation and everywhere more of these  unpleasant crawling fleshy things  slithering around the remnants of the  recent carnage it was clear to even  scp-173 that the world had changed in  some fundamental way but the hows and  whys remain just as unclear as they did  back in site-19 that's humans for you  they always know how to mess something  up speaking of it was at that moment  that scp-173 noticed a human in the  distance standing in the shade of a  ruined storefront their arms were filled  with valuables perhaps from a less than  legal shopping spree in whatever  building that used to be a wonderful  opportunity for crunch there were maybe  a hundred or so feet between the human  and 173 and it knew the second the human  looked away it would be easy to close  the distance and deliver one more sad  soul into the void with a playful little  twist the humans stepped out from the  darkness of the broken storefront and  into the light turning their ignorant  gaze away from this singularly sinister  statue yes  yes perfect in a flash 173 closed half  the distance the human was moving so  slowly it would be so easy to catch up  one more flash and it was standing right  behind the human its concrete arms  wrapped around the hapless human's head  squeeze and of course twist but no  crunch  scp-173 was startled nothing broke there  was only this quiet to almost  imperceptible squishing noise as the  head of the human twisted around 180  degrees to stare into whatever past for  scp-173's face it saw that even in what  should have been death the human was  just grinning placidly but that's the  most frightening part 173 realized that  this human wasn't dead it was just  changing it saw the facial features  starting to lose definition melting and  dripping away like candle wax in the hot  sun moments later what was once human  was now something entirely different it  melted away into another one of those  slippery slithering pseudo mollusks and  crawled away into the street somehow  completely indifferent to scp-173's  attempt on its life there was no fear no  death no  crunch for the first time in its long  and terrible existence the sculpture  couldn't help but feel a little afraid  once again it didn't fully understand  what was going on here but whatever had  changed in this world had taken away  crunch it had taken away the thing that  made the pathetic sham that some might  call life worth living for scp-173  but it wasn't going to give up that  easily no  crunch had to still be out there  somewhere this was what began as cp  173's odyssey into this horrible new  world the world in the aftermath of what  the scp foundation began to call  scp-001 when daybreaks it was the most  dangerous and horrifying anomaly that  the foundation had ever faced a  successful xk class end of the world  scenario for all intents and purposes it  had been so sudden and total any  exposure to the sun would cause a victim  to begin to melt taking on an  irreversible gelatinous state billions  were gone  changed in the first hours of this  terrible new world it led to the  administrator of the scp foundation  releasing an internal memo that would  haunt the dreams of all those still  capable of dreaming those of you with  families or god forbid children i'm  deeply deeply sorry you must push on do  not let their deaths be in vain we do  still have time humanity may still have  a future come to site 19. we need all  the hands we can get learn to embrace  the darkness friends fear the light and  this phenomenon didn't just affect  humans it affected animals and even  anomalies  scp-001 sun exposure seemed to nullify  any previous anomalous effects leading  to even some of the hardiest anomalies  melting like an ice cream cone left out  in the heat there was however one  exception to the rule inorganic  anomalies were exempt from the change  inorganic anomalies like say  a certain sculpture  scp-173 continued searching for months  on end only seeming to come up against  more maddening dead ends it traveled  from city to city with frightening speed  trying its best to track down anyone  with enough spinal integrity to produce  the crunch that made all the rest of  this terrible boredom worthwhile but no  luck every single city was more of these  flesh monsters with bones too malleable  to snap if they even still had bones at  all there was another concerning  development in all of this for scp-173  the flesh monsters were no longer just  an annoying waste of time or a symbol of  disappointment but an active nuisance to  the sculpture's goals they started  coagulating into these giant mountains  of living flesh that started actively  seeking out the last of the normal  humans from their dark crevices and  hiding places turning them into more of  those necklace jelly freaks did nobody  ever teach you animals to share  scp-173 thought angrily the seeming loss  of crunch across this new world drove  scp-173 into a deep depression it had  freedom but no joy it was a drift in a  meaningless world that seemed to exist  as some cosmic punishment for crimes it  never committed in its own mind at least  it wasn't fair none of this was fair  would the sculpture just gather dust in  an empty wasteland full of all this ugly  pointless slime and this was what it  left site 19 for and it was at that  moment that scp-173 had a wonderful  awful idea back at site 19 things  weren't exactly going swell they lost  many of their most valuable personnel  during the initial panic of scp-001  they'd been stretched to resource  capacity by the sudden influx of  refugees from this broken new world and  of course there had been the attacks all  those terrible flesh mountains were  relentless bombarding the site night  after night trying to drag people out  and expose them to the light it's why  mobile task force operatives were  stationed along the perimeter with heavy  weaponry even though short staffed as  they were these operatives were few and  far between one of them commander lewis  sat and stared into the distance keeping  an eye out for more of the flesh  mountains through the sights of his  rifle that's when he noticed a familiar  shape almost like a giant peanut since  he must be seeing things lewis rubbed  his eyes and in that moment the thing he  thought he'd seen was behind him it  snapped his neck with a familiar  satisfying crunch just as quickly just  for a moment it seemed that all was  right with the world again if scp-173  could smile it would smile and think  it's good to be back  now go check out scp-173 origin story  how 173 got to site-19 and when day  breaks  scp-096 for more of the two utterly  bizarre anomalies from today's video
 

